        "original_id": "0d829d8c-54ac-560e-a33d-f4b3e54c8d86",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Don Giovanni, Cardillac, Marzemino, Lagrein\n- People: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Lorenzo Da Ponte, Paul Hindemith\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, wine grape relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Don Giovanni is an opera in two acts with music by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart and an Italian libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte.\n- Don Giovanni has the complete title \"Il dissoluto punito, ossia il Don Giovanni,\" meaning \"The Rake Punished, namely Don Giovanni\" or \"The Libertine Punished.\"\n- Cardillac is an opera by Paul Hindemith in three acts and four scenes.\n- Marzemino is a wine noted for being mentioned in Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera Don Giovanni.\n- Lagrein, along with Marzemino, is a descendant of Teroldego and is related to Syrah, Pinot noir, and Dureza.",
